  "issues": [
    {
      "issue": "Crafting a light_gray_bed requires knowing one of two non-obvious multi-step recipes: either (A) white_wool + light_gray_dye → light_gray_wool, then 3 light_gray_wool + 3 oak_planks → bed, or (B) 3 white_wool + 3 oak_planks → white_bed, then white_bed + light_gray_dye → light_gray_bed. Neither recipe is intuitive without Minecraft crafting knowledge.",
      "severity": "medium",
      "target_agent": "TaskSelectorAgent"
    },
    {
      "issue": "The player must know to right-click (use action) on a sheep while holding shears to shear it. This is a Minecraft-specific interaction that isn't universally obvious, though it is a common game mechanic.",
      "severity": "medium",
      "target_agent": "TaskSelectorAgent"
    },
    {
      "issue": "The find_white_wool milestone (≥3) may trigger simultaneously with shear_sheep (≥1) if the first sheep drops 3 wool (which happens ~14% of the time with uniform 1-3 distribution). This would collapse two milestones into one event.",
      "severity": "low",
      "target_agent": "both"
    },
    {
      "issue": "The task_text mentions 'combine wool with light gray dye to make light gray wool' which explicitly tells the player the recipe. This is good — it mitigates the crafting knowledge requirement. However, the exact grid placement (shapeless vs shaped) still requires some familiarity with the crafting UI.",
      "severity": "low",
      "target_agent": "TaskSelectorAgent"
    }
  ],
  "approved": true,
  "critique_for_task_selector": "The benchmark is well-designed after revisions. The multi-step crafting recipe (wool→dyed wool→bed OR wool→bed→dyed bed) requires Minecraft crafting knowledge, but this is acceptable for a crafting-focused benchmark. The task_text helpfully hints at the recipe. No changes needed.",
  "critique_for_scene_designer": "The 3-sheep solution properly addresses the wool RNG issue. The scene is compact, well-lit (lantern), and navigable. One minor note: the sheep are summoned at Y=0 on top of grass_block at Y=-1, which is correct (they'll stand on the grass). No changes needed.",
  "summary": "The revised benchmark is approved. The critical wool RNG issue has been resolved by summoning 3 sheep. The milestone differentiation (≥1 vs ≥3 white_wool) creates meaningful progression, though there's a small chance (~14%) both trigger simultaneously if the first sheep drops 3 wool. The crafting knowledge requirement is medium-severity but acceptable for a crafting-focused task — the task_text provides recipe hints. The scene is well-designed with clear visibility of all objectives. All remaining issues are medium or low severity and do not block approval."
}
```
